worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/fa_invariant_cond_analysis.md:20:**Mechanism accounting:** EMA-vs-online ≤15%; effective-batch noise ~35–40% (measured by the R1→R1b delta); lr excluded (5e-6 is 8× below the original's final InverseLR value). **Leading unfalsified suspects:** (a) fresh Adam second-moment transient — the released artifact has no optimizer state, and bias-corrected steps in the first ~100s of steps take outsized parameter-relative moves at any lr; (b) drift between the code that trained the released checkpoint and this repo's training path (the config parity audit covers the config, not the code lineage). The T60/EDT-specific damage with intact retrieval suggests the energy-decay envelope is the sharpest direction of the loss landscape.
