worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_22_loc_meshgrid_claude/loc_meshgrid_worklog.md:305:- **Decisions taken and disclosed for the Planner (each reversible)** — (1) "digest mismatch" = a PIN: `meshgrid_report.REGISTERED_RETRIEVAL_HANDOFF_SHA256 = 1bf62c05…` (the bytes the canonical P1 probe consumed); alternative: an `--expect-retrieval-handoff-sha256` flag. The report beside the handoff is not re-hashed at consumption (authenticated through the pinned handoff; a test proves the committed pair agrees). (2) A crossarm without a reconciled handoff is NON-CANONICAL as a whole (Codex: "require the handoff for canonical … crossarm reports"); its statistics are still computed and labelled diagnostics. (3) `admit_run` defers the per-arm retrieval gate; the crossarm applies it once at its own level. (4) Beyond Codex's minimal fix, `open_segment` refuses a resume at another commit before it opens a segment (fail-fast; the census remains the authority). (5) Every segment counts for the one-pin rule, including one that produced no row (amendment A2 says "launch-record segments"). (6) The helpers were written in `meshgrid_offgrid_probe.py` next to the reviewed ones (outside the brief's file list, per its "write it next to them"); `read_retrieval_handoff`'s output is unchanged and pinned. (7) The static `CONTROLS_ELSEWHERE` retrieval text is now status-neutral, so FUTURE off-grid probe NPZ labels and case files carry it; the published P1 artifacts are not regenerated (the P1 phase's reconciliation stands). (8) The code-line counter used for the ledger is a scratchpad script (AST: docstrings excluded, prose constants counted) — it reproduces the R2-A ledger rows; under the universal-review rule it should be batched into the next review or the reviewer recounts independently.
