worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_22_loc_meshgrid_claude/loc_meshgrid_worklog.md:741:- **Ambiguities resolved (each a reading, disclosed)** — (a) "stamp each fa row with that segment's cumulative `n_queries` and counts digest": the stamp lives BESIDE the row (cycle 6) because `meshgrid_crossarm.PAIRING_WHITELIST` (protected) refuses any new row field; equivalent against Codex's probe (both need a coordinated ledger + one-file edit); the in-row form needs a one-line whitelist entry in the protected module — the Planner's choice, not made. (b) "admitting ONLY a single one-query-ahead state at reopen … and exact equality at merge": per segment against its own last row; at a merge the LAST invocation of each shard must be exact, an earlier crashed segment stays one ahead (bound by its prefix) and is admitted only if every call shape of its lost attempt was executed again later — a literal "every segment exact at merge" would refuse every crash-and-resume shard (D-R2-6). (c) "Refuse a missing fa ledger (and a missing summary block) whenever …": a missing ledger, with or without its summary, in a non-fresh out-dir; a missing SUMMARY beside a ledger stays admitted at a reopen. (d) "only a genuinely fresh out-dir": absent, or holding only top-level `*.json` files no pass writes (the registered lines emit `<shard>/launch_record.json` before the first run); to keep a first invocation admissible, the driver opens (and writes) the ledger BEFORE the binding and `run_pass` adopts it. (e) "the merged ledger written by the merge must pass `read_fa_ledger(merged_dir, declared, exact=True)`": a directory publishing `merge_report.json` is read in MERGED mode — joined to the receipt, never reopened (no run summary is written into a merged directory). (f) "a non-null fa receipt block, is a named refusal; an absent one is the only admitted state": absent OR null is admitted (every YAW merge writes null; the Aug-2026 P1 run has no key). (g) "Autocast clause: check the EXACT resolved state against `inputs.device`": the registered A4 clause of G1 / G3 / G3D; G2 / G0 / GV keep publishing the state without a value clause, as before (type-checked by the schema; their token is pinned by identity) — so the 14:20:53 description "for G1, G3 and G3D … also a verdict clause" still holds. (h) "`inputs_reasons` requires the exact registered DiT-input key set": enforced in the LIVE comparison too, so a live PASS always re-verifies. (i) "every per-key delta and every score delta … a finite number": finite AND non-negative (a |diff| is never negative), the two agreement flags booleans, live and re-verified. (j) The sweep "→ a non-empty reason list" needed the full schema: exact key sets, JSON types (a bool is never an int, an int never a float), the registered note / reverify_note. (k) A zero-count counts row is refused as non-canonical (a call shape no recorder observed would still move the executed block's maxima). (l) "remove it only after the check passed": a failed check leaves the sentinel beside the failure marker (both refuse; the marker is named first). (m) Mutation coverage "every new clause … AND the existing re-verifier paths": where an rB-F2 tamper was also caught by a second clause, an isolating tamper was added first, so each of the 70 deletions is observable on its own.
