worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:33:| 24 | `d40f125` | batched re-review fixes — **NEW-1** the wrapper could never succeed (`PROBE_RC=…; TEE_RC="${PIPESTATUS[1]}"` — the first assignment resets `PIPESTATUS`, `set -u` then killed it with exit 127), fixed by an atomic array capture and proven by a new shell guard test that extracts and runs the wrapper's real block (10 cases); **NEW-2** CUDA required (no silent CPU/fp32 masquerading as the bf16 qualification), `device=` emitted and wrapper-checked; **NEW-3** exact `idx:relpath` record identities (the old ones were eight identical `Cafe` labels) with distinctness enforced in probe and wrapper; **NEW-4** the stochastic contract test now models the real per-(forward × coordinate) DINO draw topology and the gradient test isolates the orbit's contribution; **NEW-5** bf16 deviations in the `EQUIVPROBE` line; **NEW-6** vanilla rows are `orbit_execution='n/a'`; **prior-7** `batch_size`/`n_samples` in the metrics record and `orbit_execution`/`frame_avg_fwd_cap`/`source_sha` added to the exp_02 comparator's guarded keys |
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:60:| 51 | `9ce96a3` | **VANL (2/3 + 3/3)** — vanilla eval protocol and table row. Screen: ARM=VANL runs `--cond-method vanilla` with NO `--frame-avg-angles` at all, eval-names `exp11_VANL_{screen,conf}_S<step>_s<seed>_K<k>`, and the ckpt-identity gate proves an ABSENCE (an orbit checkpoint dropped into the VANL tree is refused); r3 and cross are refused for VANL because orbit-shaped questions do not apply to a model with no orbit. Validator: VANL registered with orbit `None`, `orbit_for` → `[]`, run prefix `outputs_FLAC/exp11_VANL/`; the four protocol-specific record fields are lifted out of the shared mandatory tuple and asserted per-protocol — `cond_method vanilla`, `orbit_execution 'n/a'` (NEW-6), no forward cap, no angles in record or sidecar. Generator: a distinctly labelled row pair `"fa-recipe vanilla VANL @40k (exp_11 baseline)" / "vanilla eval (batched-era)"`, kept apart from the legacy vanilla rows because VANL-vs-C4L is frame averaging alone while VANL-vs-legacy still carries the bridge shift. Also: the guard suite now parks a live campaign pin for its submitter cases (the operator's pin was landing every mocked submission on `0c6e9ff` instead of HEAD). 141/141 guard cases, 218 pytest. |
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:68:| 57 | `557af4a` | **Fix 5 (figure half) — the band is harvested through the validator, and the scale spans it.** RED (`fa_orbit_2026-08-10_02-19-46_bandharvest_repro.log`): five copies of ONE seed, with valid sidecars, became a published band under the HEAD generator — `BAND STEPS: [45000] … T60 12.000 +- 1.581 (built from 5 files that are ONE seed)` — and the plotted range `(8.202, 8.993)` excluded it (`band needs <= 10.419 and >= 13.581 => band OUTSIDE the plotted scale`). Same fixture now yields `BAND STEPS: []`. Every >40k step goes through `validate_cell(..., contract="traj")` (five unique seeds, one ckpt/config/source SHA/commit/orbit_execution, 2,500 grid, >40000 floor, 100000 ceiling); a step with any problem is refused WHOLE and disclosed in the page and on stdout. Both generators scale from one `value_extent()` — points + conf whiskers + band envelope — and the PNG side calls `set_ylim` with it instead of trusting autoscale. Table view: 5-seed rows carry `mean ± sd [lo, hi]`, plus a `source` column and the four-headers-for-six-columns fix. Regenerated: 57 screen points, 5 conf endpoints, 0 validated trajectory points; only numeric movement is the T60 floor 7.92 → 7.90 (the conf whisker that was outside the scale). 18 new tests. |
