I found three provenance failures that the current tests do not cover: the registered H35 pin is user-overridable; the collector validates a receipt and then the wrapper consumes a separately reread receipt without revalidating that snapshot; and the CANON manifest is hash-checked but then reparsed from a second file read. These do not explain any current readback mismatch—the logged real artifacts are consistent—but they violate the requested fail-closed contract, so the verdict will be REQUEST-CHANGES.
Static review is complete. Three provenance/fail-closed defects require changes; all other requested checks and the evidence audit are reconciled.
  ✓ Confirm repository state, commit range, changed paths, trailers, and diff hygiene
  ✓ Read binding plan, coder brief, implementation, and tests
  ✓ Audit supplied regression/readback logs and hashes
  ✓ Cross-check K1–K8 and issue ranked findings
  ✓ Deliver K9 verdict with exact probes and readiness assessment
